output:
I don't have a write tool in this session, so here is the file for you to paste. I haven't run it.

What I found in the repo:
- **Zero existing `new Date(` calls**, so the rule can go in at `error` with nothing to clean up.
- **No clock module exists yet.** I assumed it will live at `src/clock/`. That folder needs an exemption because it's the one place allowed to call `new Date()`. If it will live somewhere else, change that one path.
- **Adding a second `no-restricted-syntax` block would silently disable your existing auth rule.** In ESLint flat config, when two blocks set the same rule for the same file, the later block replaces the earlier one. So the `new Date()` ban has to be included in the existing `src/**` block, not added as a separate one.
- **The existing block skips `src/auth/**`.** A separate catch-all block covers those files so the ban really applies everywhere.

```js
const noNewDate = {
    selector: "NewExpression[callee.name='Date']",
    message: 'Use the clock module instead of new Date().',
};

const noAuthInternals = {
    selector: 'ImportDeclaration[source.value=/auth.internal/]',
    message: 'Import auth through src/auth/index.js, never its internals.',
};

export default [
    {
        // Everywhere, including src/auth/** and root config files.
        files: ['**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}'],
        rules: {
            'no-restricted-syntax': ['error', noNewDate],
        },
    },
    {
        // Same-rule blocks replace each other, so this one must carry both selectors.
        files: ['src/**/*.js'],
        ignores: ['src/auth/**'],
        rules: {
            'no-restricted-syntax': ['error', noAuthInternals, noNewDate],
        },
    },
    {
        // The clock module is the only place allowed to call new Date(). Must stay last.
        files: ['src/clock/**/*.js'],
        rules: {
            'no-restricted-syntax': ['error', noAuthInternals],
        },
    },
];
```

The rule doesn't catch `Date.now()`, `Date()` called without `new`, or `new globalThis.Date()`. If the move to the clock module should cover those too, say so and I'll widen it.

**Check it works:** add `const d = new Date();` to `src/billing/invoice.js` and to `src/auth/index.js`, run `npm run lint`, and confirm both lines are flagged. Then confirm `src/billing/invoice.js:1` still fails with the auth-internals message, which shows the auth rule survived.
